WEBVTT

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.080
Udo, share this with everyone.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.050
Are you sure?

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:28.320
I haven't absorbed as many
Personas as everyone else.

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:29.790
Still...

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.950
Take them.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.330
Do you wanna be like Wakasa?

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.430
Any updates, Sotaro?

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.240
The exchange is today.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.960
He's going to announce the time and place.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:51.470
I'll go, so let me know when you find out.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.240
Sorry 'bout that.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.410
Anyway, I'll be taking those.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.720
You used to give that look to Wakasa, too.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:04.490
Even though he's your real brother.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.960
We'll get a bulk of them soon.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:23.180
Oh ware izukoe
Oh, where am I?

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:28.880
Oh ware yobukoe
Oh, the voice that's calling me

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.690
umetsukusu jouhou
Immersing information

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:37.060
ikigurushii kono joukyou
This suffocating situation

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.930
jibun ga inai
I'm not here

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.270
kono sekai no bousou
The world is going out of control

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:48.670
tada musekinin ni toubou
Run away irresponsibly

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:51.710
dokoe ikuno
Where am I going?

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:54.340
Huriyamanu ameni
The never-ending rain

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:58.110
zubunure oitekareta kokoro ga
Soak the neglected heart

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:03.020
kuzure yuku chokuzen no koe wo kike
Listen to the voices before it collapses

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:08.720
sasayakana kizunade ii
I'm fine with the subtle connection

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:14.700
sotto anata wo dakishimeru kara
I will hold you gently

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:26.410
kasaneta inochi ga
yukkurito ima kokyuu shite iru
The overlapped souls breathe slowly

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:30.080
sobani iruyo
"I'll be by your side."

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:35.950
Oh ware izukoe
Oh, where am I?

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:41.680
Oh ware yobukoe
Oh, the voice that's calling me

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.960
Basically, they want us to fight
using our Personas, right?

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:59.160
We don't have a choice if there's no one else.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.010
I mean, that was my initial intention anyway.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.810
Have you been training?

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:09.210
Um, no, not recently...

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:13.190
H-he just won't listen to me.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:18.490
He's so rowdy... But if it comes to it...

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.930
Shin, what about you?

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:27.800
Hey, Shin?

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:32.930
Oh, about lunch? What should we do?

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.110
Inui-san wants us to gather.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.580
I thought you were gonna let
us think it over for a few days.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:49.550
This is an unexpected situation.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.260
He's... the guy whose kids got kidnapped before.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.970
The President of Hiiragi
Pharmaceutical, Hiiragi Kazuhiko.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:08.270
And the Board of Directors head, Nagai Kiyohumi.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:18.440
Both were involved in the Persona research by
some organization and special force project with us.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:24.820
Half a year ago, former chief of
Ayanagi Police Station, Kanzato Ryo,

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:28.160
and Dr. Nikaido Eiko, left evidence.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:40.010
From it, we discovered Hiiragi Pharmaceutical was
continuing development of Persona control pills.

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:45.570
Instead of bringing charges upon them,
we made a deal with President Hiiragi.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:53.020
We were going to have him lure out the people
who need the drugs, the Marebito, with his name.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:05:00.720
However, the exchange halted due
to the former chief's warnings.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.870
And before the Marebito
requested it to be re-opened...

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.230
The incident from a few days ago happened.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:17.870
They don't know... where to get the drugs.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:25.540
Looks like the exchange was being
done by Kujo, the Marebito's leader.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:28.680
However, he can't be located at the moment.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:32.520
The Marebito are reaching their limit.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:38.900
If they don't have their lifeline, we should
just wait for them to perish naturally.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:44.400
Depending on the situation, that
may cause more civilian sacrifices.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:54.110
Plus, not only the Marebito, but unless we
locate Kujo, this problem will not be solved.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:06:01.340
Apparently, Nagai was carrying something out of
the lab, which is now closed down, this morning.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:07.450
Most likely the pills, which they
were ordered to dispose of.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:13.500
We have no idea why Nagai, Hiiragi's
trusted underling, is acting on his own...

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:16.870
or how he contacted the Marebito.

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:21.470
It seems there's a possibility they
will have their exchange today.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:26.350
Ito-san, have you heard anything
more from Detective Narasaki?

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:31.340
Apparently, he drove towards Takayama and
strayed from the National Highway near Yatsuo.

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:40.060
I wanted to wait until we were ready,
but the plan has been put on fast-forward.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:44.100
On that note, I'd like to say one more
thing before hearing your decisions.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:49.970
Our request doesn't necessarily
demand you fight with your Personas,

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:51.730
and neither it is compulsory.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:56.140
However, you guys are the
only ones who can fight them.

00:06:57.210 --> 00:07:02.740
And... if we were to battle, the enemies
will use everything they've got.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:08.580
This...

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:13.020
This is ridiculous!

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:18.490
What is this!? You keep going on and on
without even stopping to ask our opinions!

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.000
Kayano...

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.070
We're just normal high schoolers.

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:25.870
We have to study for college and
participate in club activities...

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:33.350
That aside... How do you expect us
to fight against such bad people!?

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:35.610
Hey, Megumi...

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:40.550
I agree with her, though.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:44.790
This came up so suddenly... it's overwhelming.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:48.190
Plus... I'm not fully convinced, myself.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:51.920
What she's saying is right.

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:55.330
But... it doesn't mean something
like this hasn't happened before.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:59.070
We can't wait long to find the specific location.

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:01.040
Prepare to leave for Yatsuo.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:01.930
Yes.

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:19.160
Are you gonna do it?

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:19.850
Yes.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:26.560
I've been thinking about my brother.

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.000
This is the decision I came to.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:31.370
I see.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:34.570
I just have to wait in my room, right?

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.070
Yeah.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:18.480
I'm sure what that guy says is the truth.

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:23.290
But you're basically gonna be
used as a weapon, you know?

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:25.220
You're right.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:29.900
But this is what aniki was trying to do.

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:34.960
There are people trying to distort the power
of Personas and use them for something bad...

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.860
and he was trying to stop them.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.200
That's all, right?

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:45.550
He joined the police, became a chief, and...

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:47.780
he even established a special force.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:52.550
Yet, none of it helped.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:58.050
He could've talked to us about it a little.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:02.690
The three of us are the only family we've got...

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:06.300
Niichan...

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:25.880
Sakakiba-kun, our break is almost over.

00:10:29.090 --> 00:10:32.180
H-hey, how did that get on your glasses?

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:43.000
We're the only ones who can fight them, huh?

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:45.670
What are you talking about?

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:48.380
Sorry, I'm gonna take off.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.010
Can you tell our manager?

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:52.680
What? You were late and you're leaving early?

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:54.480
I also have to...

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:57.080
I was asked to run an errand for someone.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:58.980
I gotta go to Yatsuo.

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:10.590
Hey... I'm really counting on you this time.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.680
He finally gave us the location.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:23.980
Where Sugibayashi Elementary
School used to be, in Yatsuo.

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:26.640
It's good to be cautious, but
this is way off the beaten path.

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:32.250
Regardless, we're not in the position to choose
anyway. It's gonna be a big package, too.

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:35.660
Sotaro, can't we change it?

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:40.390
Nope. The condition was to follow
his orders on location and time.

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:42.060
...Is there a problem?

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:52.540
Yes. He stopped by his storage on the way, too.

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:55.370
Looked like he's taking everything that's left.

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:59.680
There were a few other locations he had in mind,

00:11:59.680 --> 00:12:02.480
but looks like he chose this
spot away from the crowd.

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:05.110
As expected, Nagai was behind all this.

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:08.020
The opposite party hasn't shown up yet.

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:13.990
Yes, I'm aware. I've come
this far. I won't let him go.

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:28.830
Ito-san, thanks for the cab.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:31.080
Of course, you can expense it, right?

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:36.520
Takuro...

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.920
I'd be too worried to let you go alone.

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:46.020
Listen, we'll trail the Marebito from the ground and
Sanada will trail from the sky after the exchange.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:53.800
Our goal is to locate their hideout. If we at
least learn the general area, that'd be fine, too.

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:54.640
What?

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:59.000
How could I possibly make you high
school kids fight against murderers?

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:05.310
Boss said fighting them wasn't necessarily
the condition, either, remember?

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:08.280
Then what was the point of us?

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:12.290
Yeah, we better beat the crap out of the Marebito.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:17.590
The better your Persona, the harder
you'll Reverse when extracted.

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:19.720
That was the logic, right?

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.360
Leave the rough play...

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:24.450
to the professio...

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:44.180
Shin, let's go.

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:45.580
B-but...

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:47.170
He's gone already.

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:04.890
Won't you let us go?

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:06.490
Can't.

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:11.430
We... can't live without these.

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:13.170
Let's go to the hospital.

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:16.070
I don't have insurance.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:21.080
It'd be hard to settle this in
court, since we don't really exist.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:23.620
Enough of this, you brat.

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:25.050
Saki...

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:38.560
Take us to your leader.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:40.700
...Sure.

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:48.740
What are we gonna do there?

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.670
Play Othello with everyone?

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:07.850
Mr. Detective... Mr. Detective.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:11.530
Your phone is going off.

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:18.470
You shouldn't be sleeping here.

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:20.740
Y-you...

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:23.610
Umm... Where are we?

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:28.150
They ambushed you guys?

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:30.980
Yeah, and I can't get a hold of Narasaki, either.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:33.750
One of them took half the supplies, too.

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:36.890
Can you see the car heading northwest?

00:16:52.410 --> 00:16:53.630
I can't confirm them.

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:55.340
That can't be...

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:58.040
I'll join you guys... How's Shin?

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.210
A-are you?

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:37.810
It's your fault for interfering.

00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:44.980
It should be quick.

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:48.990
I'm sorry, but I don't know how to go easy...

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:59.670
Oh yeah... I wonder if your power will
be mine if I absorb your Persona?

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:25.500
Takuro!

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:27.200
Shin!

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:51.450
Jun!

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:57.200
Get in!

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:08.270
Don't hurt... my brother...

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:40.660
Jun!

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:10.200
Wh-why?

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:23.180
We have to treat him fast!

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:24.810
Narasaki.

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:25.980
Morimoto!?

00:20:27.050 --> 00:20:28.040
I'm sorry...

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:29.410
Jun-kun?

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.220
Inui, gather all the control pills in one place.

00:20:33.590 --> 00:20:34.490
Y-yes.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:37.030
Sanada-san, first...

00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:38.460
They missed the vitals.

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:40.700
That won't work.

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:44.340
We've got to hurry to the hospital!

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:48.270
No, we mustn't move around
too much during the night.

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:49.610
But!

00:20:49.610 --> 00:20:51.200
They've got nothing left to lose.

00:20:51.780 --> 00:20:54.980
They won't give up on the rest of the pills so easily.

00:20:56.750 --> 00:20:57.650
Plus...

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:02.720
Dammit!

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:07.520
Megumi!?

00:21:25.210 --> 00:21:25.910
H-hey.

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:29.410
Megumi?

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:32.980
This...

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:36.020
is my parents' house.

00:21:52.270 --> 00:21:57.280
Itsukara yume miru koto
When did I start pretending
like I didn't dream of anything?

00:21:57.280 --> 00:22:03.320
Wasureta huri wo shitetan darou
When did I start pretending
like I didn't dream of anything?

00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:09.960
Chiisana mado akeru yuuki mo naku
With no courage to open a small
window, I waited for a miracle.

00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:15.230
Kiseki wo matteta
With no courage to open a small
window, I waited for a miracle.

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:24.940
Ushinau mono nado nakatta anohi no yona
I'm not as innocent as I used to be in
the days when I had nothing to lose

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:30.440
mujakisa wa mou naikedo
I'm not as innocent as I used to be in
the days when I had nothing to lose

00:22:30.440 --> 00:22:36.880
namida wo nugutta ato niwa
After wiping away the tears

00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:42.890
atarashii jibun ni deaeru
I'll be able to meet a new self

00:22:42.890 --> 00:22:46.790
subete wo nakushitemo
mitsuke rareru monoga arukara
Even if I lose everything

00:22:46.790 --> 00:22:53.000
subete wo nakushitemo
mitsuke rareru monoga arukara
There are still some things to discover

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:58.770
kesenai kizumo itsuka
Even the scars that remain

00:22:58.770 --> 00:23:05.770
watashi rashii hokori ni dekiru
will someday become my pride

00:23:10.950 --> 00:23:13.050
A patch of clouds

00:23:13.050 --> 00:23:15.920
was enough to compress a small heart.

00:23:16.760 --> 00:23:20.730
Even if you gaze straight ahead,

00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:22.920
you'll never know the truth.

00:23:24.030 --> 00:23:27.700
A heart saved by a harsh sentence.

00:23:27.700 --> 00:23:30.170
Still imprisoned by fear.

00:23:30.170 --> 00:23:32.330
Struggling to be taken.

00:23:33.110 --> 00:23:35.810
A place that's close, but far.

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:38.570
A home she did not wish to return to.
